<h2><%= @notification.title %></h2>

<p><%= @notification.body %></p>

<p><%= link_to "Open your dashboard", @url %></p>

<% if @notification.severity == "critical" %>
  <p>
    <strong>This alert concerns a running strategy.</strong> Positions may be open
    with your broker. Check your MT5 terminal.
  </p>
<% end %>

<hr>

<p style="font-size:12px;color:#64748B">
  You are receiving this because notifications are enabled on your
  <%= Rails.application.config.x.product.name %> account.
  <%= link_to "Manage notification settings", URI.join(root_url, "/settings/notifications").to_s %>.
  Alerts about a terminal that has stopped reporting cannot be switched off,
  because a running strategy with no terminal is not a state you should
  discover by accident.
</p>
